   "spoken": "Take the pawn — no calculation needed, just see the pin and the loose rook. Then Bxf3 is the instructive move: strategically it hands over our fine bishop, but tactically it's justified, clearing the e-file to hit the uncastled king with Qe5-check hitting the king and the knight. Chess is a constant interplay between the strategic and the concrete.",
